From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Date: Sun, 03 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] amdgpu/uapi,object: add PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR GEM create flag

Patch 1 added a lazy eviction path in amdgpu_dma_buf_map() so that a
VRAM BO is automatically moved to GTT when the GPU lacks large BAR and
an importer tries to DMA-map it.  That eviction happens at the point the
DMA-BUF is first mapped by an NVMe (or similar) device — meaning the BO
has already been allocated in VRAM and must be copied to GTT before the
first transfer can begin.  On busy systems this serializes the very first
transfer and briefly doubles the memory footprint.

Introduce AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR (bit 17 of the GEM
create flags) to let callers declare upfront that a BO will be used for
DMA-BUF P2P I/O on a system that may lack resizable BAR.  When the flag
is set and visible_vram_size < real_vram_size, amdgpu_bo_placement_from_
domain() redirects the effective placement from VRAM to GTT before the
placement-building loop runs.  The BO is therefore allocated in GTT from
the outset; no eviction is needed at DMA-BUF map_attachment time.

On large-BAR systems (visible_vram_size == real_vram_size) the flag is
silently ignored and the normal VRAM placement policy applies.

Intended users:
  * The ROCm / HIP runtime, which can set this flag when allocating device
    memory buffers the application will use as io_uring DMA-BUF targets
    (the "hipfile" use-case).
  * Direct users of the amdgpu GEM ioctls, such as the test program in
    userspace/amdgpu-dmabuf-io/, that want deterministic up-front placement
    rather than relying on the lazy eviction fallback introduced by patch 1.

Bit 17 is chosen to avoid collisions with current upstream flags (bits
0-16, noting that GFX12_DCC occupies bit 16).

Signed-off-by: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
---
--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
@@ -115,6 +115,17 @@
 	u64 flags = abo->flags;
 	u32 c = 0, i;
 
+	/*
+	 * On no-large-BAR systems redirect upfront VRAM allocations to GTT when
+	 * the caller sets PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR.  This avoids the eviction
+	 * overhead in amdgpu_dma_buf_map() for callers that know their BO will
+	 * be used as an io_uring DMA-BUF P2P target.
+	 */
+	if ((flags & AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR) &&
+	    adev->gmc.real_vram_size > adev->gmc.visible_vram_size &&
+	    (domain & AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM))
+		domain = (domain & ~AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM) | AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_GTT;
+
 	if (domain & AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM) {
 		unsigned int visible_pfn = adev->gmc.visible_vram_size >> PAGE_SHIFT;
 		int8_t mem_id = KFD_XCP_MEM_ID(adev, abo->xcp_id);
--- a/include/uapi/drm/amdgpu_drm.h
+++ b/include/uapi/drm/amdgpu_drm.h
@@ -189,6 +189,13 @@
 #define AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_EXT_COHERENT		(1 << 15)
 /* Set PTE.D and recompress during GTT->VRAM moves according to TILING flags. */
 #define AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_GFX12_DCC		(1 << 16)
+/*
+ * Prefer GTT placement on systems without resizable BAR (large BAR / ReBAR).
+ * When set and visible_vram_size < real_vram_size, amdgpu allocates the BO in
+ * GTT rather than VRAM so it is always reachable by peer DMA devices (e.g.
+ * NVMe via io_uring DMA-BUF).  Silently ignored on large-BAR systems.
+ */
+#define AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR	(1 << 17)
 
 /* hybrid specific */
 /* Flag that the memory should be in SPARSE resource */
